# An unknown HEADER key is reported, once per key per load (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 3.2, macos
# 2026-10-11).  The header chain's final ELSE was a bare GO TO 50: an unknown key -- a typo
# included -- was dropped with NO message (the element chain has always said 'Unidentified
# string').  That is how OptMxItrs= silently lost the cap.  tst_hdr_unknown.in carries the
# corpus misspelling OpdReRayfLen= TWICE and SegYgrid= once: two lines, not three.  The deck
# still loads (warn, never refuse).  Pre-fix: no line at all -- red.
# OptFooKey= (2026-10-12, PLAN 1.1b): a LOOK-ALIKE the warning could not see -- the header chain
# matched OptFOVWt on 5 characters ('OptFo'), so any OptFo* key was read as FOV weights.  Every
# header match is now the full key name (23 lengthened; no deck in the 1353-deck extended corpus
# nor any binding writer uses a shorter or variant spelling), so it is reported.  Red on e8c80ea.
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_hdr_unknown.in
# EXPECT: MBFile6: Unidentified header string = OpdReRayfLen
# EXPECT: MBFile6: Unidentified header string = SegYgrid
# EXPECT: MBFile6: Unidentified header string = OptFooKey
# EXPECT: Tracing rays past\s+2\s+elements
# EXPECT-NOT: Unidentified header string = OpdReRayfLen[\s\S]*Unidentified header string = OpdReRayfLen
